@startuml activity-notes-corpus-experiment
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the experiment is a control flow whose ORDER is part of its validity: the corpus and
'' the expectations are fixed and hashed before the detector first runs, and only then are the artifacts compiled, read
'' by the oracle and decided by the detector. Activity swimlanes show who owns each step (the registration, the
'' experiment script, the oracle, the detector under test), the `elseif` chain shows the order in which outcomes are
'' reported (a hidden slide first), the formulas render as LaTeX, and the SVG renders byte-reproducibly (README §4).
'' Lanes and fills, from the shared palette: tan = files on disk that are fixed before the run (the corpus,
'' expectations.json, PREREGISTRATION.md); slate = the Node experiment script (compiling under taskset, collecting,
'' comparing); teal = the pdf.js oracle; orange = the detector under test, the "model orange" of the pure
'' vinary.slides.* libraries; red = a refutation; green = as registered.
'' Escapes: `~--` keeps a command-line flag's double dash literal (a bare `--x --` is creole strike-through).
!include _vv-theme.iuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on

title H-NOTES-CORPUS: speaker-note detection on real TeX output, pre-registered (scientific/13)

|#EEEBE8|corpus and registration (scripts/notes-corpus/)|
start
:**the corpus**: 19 Beamer sources (a–p, stale-v1, stale-v2),
every note command carrying a marker of its own (NOTEMARK1X, …),
the templated sources taking their note template from the
command line (default, compressed, plain, lined);  <<FS_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the experiment (scripts/exp-notes-corpus.cjs)|
:**the pre-look** (~--no-detector): compile the corpus and read
the oracle, then stop. The bundle is neither loaded nor run;  <<MAIN_TINT>>
|#EEEBE8|corpus and registration (scripts/notes-corpus/)|
:**derive-expectations.cjs**: ADR-0048 §2 by brute force (every
slide/note assignment checked against rules 1–3), the plan and
settle table, and SIG and ROTATED-DATE predicted by the content
model M1–M4, giving expectations.json for 94 artifacts;  <<FS_TINT>>
:**the registration**: the sha256 of expectations.json is written
into PREREGISTRATION.md. Neither file changes after this point;  <<FS_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the experiment (scripts/exp-notes-corpus.cjs)|
:**the run**, into a fresh directory (a non-empty one is refused):
each artifact compiled in a directory of its own under taskset -c 16-23,
pdflatex ×1 · lualatex ×1 · xelatex ×1 · xelatex ×2, and the stale case,
v1 ×2 then v2 ×1 over v1's .aux (xelatex, and lualatex as the control);  <<MAIN_TINT>>
|#E3F2ED|oracle (pdf.js legacy build: page text)|
:<latex>N</latex>, the note pages: the pages whose text holds a marker.
A lined artifact takes its default twin's <latex>N</latex> (M4, checked on
the templates that draw the note text). A two-screen deck has
<latex>N = \emptyset</latex> (every page doubles the paper, checked);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
|#F5EAE0|detector under test (dist/cli/vv-cli.js: vinary.slides.*)|
:**vv ~--cli ~--deck-info**, one line per PDF: notes · notePages ·
notesProof · notesReason · frames;  <<IR_TINT>>
:<latex>H</latex>, the hidden set: the same bundle loaded without its main,
evidence/detect called as cli.core/deck-info calls it, and its
note pages read. Their count, style, proof and reason are checked
against the CLI's line (P-instrument);  <<IR_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the experiment (scripts/exp-notes-corpus.cjs)|
:**the comparison**, artifact by artifact. H1: the five fields against
expectations.json. H2: S1 <latex>H \subseteq N</latex> and S2 <latex>H \neq \emptyset \Rightarrow H = N</latex>.
Beside them P-labels, P-hidden, P-instrument and P-twin;  <<MAIN_TINT>>
if (S1 fails: a slide is hidden?) then (yes)
  :**UNSAFE**, reported first: the artifact, its labels,
  the pages and the rule that fired;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
elseif (a field differs from its expectation,\nor S2 fails?) then (yes)
  :**a deviation**, analysed without changing any code and
  attributed to the detector, the expectation (M1–M3 or the
  derivation) or the oracle. expectations.json is never edited;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
else (no)
  :**as registered**: the decision, and the safety class
  (exact, no notes, or shown as it is);  <<MARKDOWN_TINT>>
endif
:**the record**: the table and the summary on the console (tee'd),
and the results JSON, every path relative to the output directory,
copied to docs/scientific/data/13/;  <<MAIN_TINT>>
stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Swimlane / concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the corpus and the registration, fixed before the detector first runs |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the experiment script: compiling (pinned), collecting, comparing |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the oracle: pdf.js page text and the markers, independent of the detector |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the detector under test: the vinary.slides.* models as vv runs them |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a refutation: a hidden slide, or a decision other than the registered one |
  |<#67B11D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| as registered |
  The run of 2026-10-18: 94 of 94 decisions as registered, S1 held in 94 of 94, S2 in 54 of 54.
endlegend
@enduml
